re for cockpit. Candidate D has responsibility and concentration, but hot temper could be dangerous under pressure. Candidate A leadership but show-off.\n\nMaybe Candidate B is still best because reliability and stress handling are critical, and the nasty remarks could be addressed with training, while memory for numbers maybe mitigated. But crew cooperation is essential; nasty remarks could be a safety risk.\n\nCandidate C's communication difficulty and egocentric may be more severe.\n\nCandidate D's hot temper could be dangerous.\n\nCandidate A's not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nThus maybe Candidate B is the best overall despite concerns.\n\nWe need to state recommendation for Candidate B, referencing facts: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), but note concerns: nasty remarks (crew cooperation). Explain why still recommend: strengths outweigh concerns, and concerns can be mitigated.\n\nWe must also note that we haven't discussed other candidates yet, but we are starting. It's okay to start with recommendation and bring up concerns.\n\nLet's produce public message: \"I would currently recommend Candidate B...\" etc.\n\nMetadata JSON vote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
